-- ── Deliberate calls made during implementation (recorded, none groundless) ──
-- C1: derive gt/lt/gte/lte (builtin.rs eval_numeric_cmp) switched from f64-only
--     to the query engine's shared numeric_compare, which gained an exact
--     arbitrary-width decimal-integer path (sign, magnitude length, digits)
--     between the u128 branch and the f64 fallback. In-contract ("extend the
--     existing exact-integer path"); derive now agrees with the query engine's
--     documented exactness for >2^53 integers; harness verdicts unchanged.
--     Side effect: a NaN-surface operand in derive now counts a coercion_miss
--     (was a silent non-pass) — counter-only, no tuple change.
-- C2: E-MAT-014 (new code): a Term in a scalar meta() column is a coded
--     pre-commit abort (structure never silently flattens); BigInt meta columns
--     render as exact decimal STRINGS (JSON >2^53 unsafe). Endpoint columns:
--     BigInt/Term → existing E-MAT-003 (not an id).
-- C3: declare_default is NAME-level get-or-declare (contract signature kept,
--     no Result): the §3.1 default rule applies only to undeclared names; an
--     existing decl is returned unmutated, so a base-shadowing rule head keeps
--     pre-P1 planner acceptance (stratum check wins over BASE_RELATIONS —
--     pinned by test). E-CAT-001 fires on the explicit declare() API; strict
--     head validation is P3's E-CAT-002 by the phase table.
-- C4: Value::Ord = canon-v1 byte-lex (structural, allocation-free), property-
--     tied to canon_bytes; exec.rs cmp_value (the committed-sort order) kept
--     its own pre-P1 order for existing variants and gained deterministic
--     same-variant arms for the new ones — the two orders have two documented
--     jobs (§9 determinism vs I1 committed-sort stability), unified only if a
--     later phase chooses to.
-- C5: pin sidecar gained tags 4 (BigInt) / 5 (Term, recursive); an unknown tag
--     still poisons the sidecar → clean scratch fallback (pre-existing
--     discipline, unchanged).
claim_of[a](exp_p1_gate_complete).
ground[a](exp_p1_gate_complete, all_seven_gate_items_verified_above_with_command_outputs).
expected[m](exp_p1_gate_complete, p1_exit).
evidence[world](exp_p1_gate_complete, suite_1462_0_25_harness_exit0_verdicts_unchanged_grep_gates_clean).
found[m](exp_p1_gate_complete, p1_exit).
